From: r11234567 <noreply@github.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 14:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Harden parser bounds and allocation failures

Fix the actionable findings reported while xquic was included in mqvpn's
CodeQL database. Keep the changes as a downstream patch until they can be
submitted to and released by xquic.

The xqc_var_buf_reduce and xqc_submatrix hunks used to live here too. They
now ship in the pinned xquic fork itself, so carrying them here as well left
this patch permanently half-applied, which fails both the reverse-check and
the forward-apply in scripts/apply_xquic_patches.sh. Any fix promoted into
the fork must be dropped from this file in the same change.

diff --git a/src/transport/scheduler/xqc_scheduler_rap.h b/src/transport/scheduler/xqc_scheduler_rap.h
--- a/src/transport/scheduler/xqc_scheduler_rap.h
+++ b/src/transport/scheduler/xqc_scheduler_rap.h
@@ -2,8 +2,8 @@
